nventory","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"2010-04-26","later-events_catalog":"2010-04-26","research/stage21/original_sources/CASE_ORIGINAL_SOURCE_CUSTODY.csv":"2010-04-26","stage19_causal_queue":"2010-04-26","stage21_crosswalk":"2010-04-26"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:13540","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Establishment. The Administrator of the Small Business Adminis-\ntration (Administrator) shall establish within the Small Business Administra-\ntion an Interagency Task Force on Veterans Small Business Development \n(Task Force).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Membership. The Administrator shall serve as Chair of the Task \nForce and shall direct its work. Other members shall consist of:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) a senior level representative, designated by the head of the respective \ndepartment or agency, from each of the following: \n(i) the Department of the Treasury; \n(ii) the Department of Defense; \n(iii) the Department of Labor; \n(iv) the Department of Veterans Affairs; \n(v) the Office of Management and Budget; \n(vi) the Small Business Administration (in addition to the Administrator); \nand \n(vii) the General Services Administration; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) four representatives from a veterans’ service or military organization \nor association, who shall be appointed by the Administrator.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Functions. Consistent with the Act and other applicable law, the \nTask Force shall:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) consult regularly with veterans service and military organizations in \nperforming the duties of the Task Force;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) coordinate administrative and regulatory activities and develop pro-\nposals relating to: \n(i) improving capital access and capacity of small business concerns owned \nand controlled by veterans and service-disabled veterans through loans, \nsurety bonding, and franchising; \n(ii) ensuring achievement of the pre-established Federal contracting goals \nfor small business concerns owned and controlled by veterans and service- \ndisabled veterans through expanded mentor-prote´ge´ assistance and match-\ning such small business concerns with contracting opportunities; \n(iii) increasing the integrity of certifications of status as a small business \nconcern owned and controlled by a veteran or service-disabled veteran; \n(iv) reducing paperwork and administrative burdens on veterans in access-\ning business development and entrepreneurship opportunities; \nVerDate Mar<15>2010 16:48 Apr 28, 2010 Jkt 220001 PO 00000 Frm 00001 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\29APE0.SGM 29APE0mstockstill on DSKH9S0YB1PROD with PRESDOCE0\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n22498 Federal Register / Vol. 75, No. 82 / Thursday, April 29, 2010 / Presidential Documents \n(v) increasing and improving training and counseling services provided \nto small business concerns owned and controlled by veterans; and \n(vi) making other improvements relating to the support for veterans busi-\nness development by the Federal Government; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) not later than 1 year after its first meeting and annually thereafter, \nforward to the President a report on the performance of its functions, includ-\ning any proposals developed pursuant to subsection (b) of this section.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Small Business Administration shall \nprovide funding and administrative support for the Task Force to the extent \npermitted by law and within existing appropriations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Nothing in this order shall be construed to impair or otherwise effect: \n(i) authority granted by law to an executive department, agency, or the \nhead thereof; and \n(ii) functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Insofar as the Federal Advisory Committee Act, as amended (5 U.S.C. \nApp.) (FACA), may apply to the Task Force, any functions of the President \nunder the FACA, except for those in section 6 of the FACA, shall be \nperformed by the Administrator in accordance with guidelines issued by \nthe Administrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) This order is not intended to and does not create any right or benefit, \nsubstantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party \nagainst the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, \nemployees, or agents, or any other person.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"75 FR 22497, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 4(d)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13540#sec4(d)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (75 FR 22497)","sha256":"b6bd4a4d0c2eae831a6e473534e1b97bcc7b8672165221c2ac6202f1ee9029ec","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2010-04-29/pdf/2010-10172.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 12 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: current legal basis not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"yes"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:13540"}
